---
title: "Flow 3 — Admin Registration (implemented: enrollment-service)"
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor Admin
    participant Client as Angular SPA
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant IAM as Identity and Access
    participant ENR as Enrollment
    participant ACAD as Academic Structure
    participant MQ as Message Broker

    Admin->>Client: Select student, select program, click "Register"
    Client->>GW: POST /students/{id}/program-enrollments {programId} (JWT)
    GW->>IAM: validate token
    IAM-->>GW: valid, role = Administrator
    GW->>ENR: forward registration, actorId = admin.id

    ENR->>ACAD: GET degree program (exists? active?)
    ACAD-->>ENR: program valid

    ENR->>ENR: insert StudentProgramEnrollment
    ENR->>ENR: insert RegistrationLog (actor = Admin, action = "program registration")
    ENR-->>GW: 201 Created
    GW-->>Client: "Student registered"
    Client-->>Admin: Shown in Recent Registrations

    ENR-)MQ: publish StudentProgramRegistered (async)

    Note over ENR: Same Enrollment write path as self-service enrollment —<br/>only the actor and the audit log entry differ.<br/>This is why "Administration" has no service of its own.
